time=2026-10-26T16:27:45.990Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-0cd78a69 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe autoMergeTree function asks git for the automatic merge of two commits and returns the merged tree id and the conflicted paths.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives a pointer to a repo and two commit revision strings, first and second, in that order\n- The function returns the merged tree id as a string, the conflicted paths as a slice of strings, and an error, in that order\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The function runs the git subcommand merge-tree with the arguments --write-tree, --name-only, the first revision and the second revision, in that order\n- The function reads only the standard output of the command and ignores its standard error\n- A command that exits with status 0 is a success\n- A command that exits with status 1, which git uses to report conflicts, is also a success and its standard output is still read\n- A command that cannot be started, or that exits with any status other than 0 or 1, makes the function return an empty string, a nil slice and a non-nil error\n- The tree id is the first line of the standard output, with surrounding whitespace removed\n- When the standard output has no first line or the first line is empty, the function returns an empty string, a nil slice and a non-nil error\n- The conflicted paths are the lines that follow the first line, one path per line, up to but not including the first empty line\n- Lines after the first empty line, which are git's informational messages, are not part of the conflicted paths\n- When there are no conflicted paths the returned slice is empty or nil and the error is nil\n- The function owns the imports of errors, os/exec and strings, each as a value import of the standard library\n- The function runs git in the directory held in the Root field of the repo\n- The function runs git with the environment slice returned by the repo gitEnv method (no parameters, returns a slice of strings)\n- The function runs git itself through the os/exec package and not through the repo git method\n- When the standard output is empty the function reports the failure with errors.New from the errors package\n- When the command cannot be started or exits with a status other than 0 or 1 the function returns the command's own error\n- With --name-only, git prints each conflicted path relative to the directory it runs in, with paths outside that directory starting with ../, and the function returns the paths as printed.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"errors\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func autoMergeTree(r *repo, first, second string) (string, []string, error) {\\n\\tcmd := exec.Command(\\\"git\\\", \\\"merge-tree\\\", \\\"--write-tree\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", first, second)\\n\\tcmd.Dir = r.Root\\n\\tcmd.Env = r.gitEnv()\\n\\tout, err := cmd.Output()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\tvar exitErr *exec.ExitError\\n\\t\\tif !errors.As(err, \\u0026exitErr) || exitErr.ExitCode() != 1 {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tlines := strings.Split(string(out), \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\\ttreeID := strings.TrimSpace(lines[0])\\n\\tif treeID == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, errors.New(\\\"merge-tree produced no tree id\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\tvar paths []string\\n\\tfor _, line := range lines[1:] {\\n\\t\\tif strings.TrimSpace(line) == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tpaths = append(paths, strings.TrimSpace(line))\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn treeID, paths, nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"name\":\"autoMergeTree\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-25b92cac; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"} (owned by prov-2026-25b92cac; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"name\":\"commitParents\"} (owned by prov-2026-06e21d9f; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"name