time=2026-10-26T16:27:56.236Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-28d0e0c4 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe stagedTree function writes the staged files under the config's directory to a temporary directory and returns the path of the config's directory inside it, so it can be read as a tree.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives a pointer to a repo (defined in common_run.go of package main) as its only argument\n- The function returns three values in order: the path of the config's directory inside the temporary directory as a string, a cleanup function taking no arguments and returning nothing, and an error\n- The function creates a temporary directory in the system temporary location\n- The temporary directory name starts with \"provenance-staged-\"\n- When the temporary directory cannot be created, the function returns an empty path, a nil cleanup function and the error\n- The function runs the repo's git method (parameters: a variadic list of string arguments; returns the trimmed standard output as a string and an error)\n- The git arguments of the checkout, in order, are: checkout-index, the all-files flag -a, and the prefix option --prefix= followed by the temporary directory path and a slash\n- The checkout runs in the repo root, so git checks out only the index files under the repo root.\n- Git writes each checked-out file under the temporary directory at its path relative to the git top level.\n- When the checkout fails, the function removes the temporary directory\n- When the checkout fails, the function returns an empty path, a nil cleanup function and the error\n- After a successful checkout the function runs the repo's git method with rev-parse and --show-prefix\n- When that command fails, the function removes the temporary directory and returns an empty path, a nil cleanup function and the error\n- With an empty prefix the returned path is the temporary directory itself\n- The function creates the returned path, with its parent directories, with os.MkdirAll and permission 0o755, because git writes nothing when the repo root has no staged files\n- When creating the returned path fails, the function removes the temporary directory and returns an empty path, a nil cleanup function and the error\n- On success the function returns the path, the cleanup function and a nil error\n- The cleanup function removes the whole temporary directory and everything under it, not only the returned path\n- That command returns the repo root relative to the git top level, with a trailing slash.\n- That command returns an empty string at the git top level.\n- Each \"/\" in the prefix is replaced by os.PathSeparator, using strings.ReplaceAll.\n- With a non-empty prefix the returned path is the string concatenation of the temporary directory, os.PathSeparator and the converted prefix, with no use of path/filepath.\n- The returned path keeps the trailing separator that comes from the prefix's trailing slash.\n- The function owns the import of os as a value import of the standard library\n- The function uses strings, whose import is owned by another record in the same file\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func stagedTree(r *repo) (string, func(), error) {\\n\\tdir, err := os.MkdirTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"provenance-staged-\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tcleanup := func() { os.RemoveAll(dir) }\\n\\tif _, err := r.git(\\\"checkout-index\\\", \\\"-a\\\", \\\"--prefix=\\\"+dir+\\\"/\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tcleanup()\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn dir, cleanup, nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"name\":\"stagedTree\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"errors\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"fmt\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/lint\"} (owned by prov-2026-8a4ab260; do not select)\n- cmd/pr