time=2026-10-26T16:28:03.816Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-55145cec attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe mergeIsAutomatic function reports whether a merge commit's tree equals git's automatic merge of its two parents.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives a pointer to a repo, a tree id string and a slice of parent commit id strings, in that order\n- The function returns a single bool\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The function returns false when the parents slice does not have exactly two entries\n- The function calls autoMergeTree (defined in the same file; parameters in order: a pointer to a repo, the first revision string, the second revision string; returns the tree id string, the conflicted paths as a slice of strings, and an error) with the repo, the first parent and the second parent\n- The function returns false when autoMergeTree returns an error\n- The function runs git through the repo git method (defined in common_run.go; parameter: variadic strings; returns trimmed standard output as a string and an error) with the arguments diff-tree, -r, --name-only, --no-renames, --relative, the automatic tree id, the given tree id, in that order\n- The --relative argument makes git print each differing path relative to the directory git runs in, which is the repo root, namely the config's directory.\n- The --relative argument makes git leave out every differing path outside that directory, so such paths do not make the merge non-automatic.\n- The function returns false when that git command fails\n- The function reads the differing paths as the non-empty lines of that command's output\n- The function returns true when no path differs between the automatic tree and the given tree\n- The function returns true only when every differing path is equal to manifestPath, the string constant of package main naming the version manifest file, and is also one of the conflicted paths returned by autoMergeTree\n- The function returns false when any differing path is not manifestPath\n- The function returns false when manifestPath differs but was not among the conflicted paths\n- The conflicted paths from autoMergeTree are relative to that same directory, because git merge-tree --name-only prints paths relative to the directory it runs in, so comparing them with manifestPath works for a config below the git top level.\n- A conflicted path outside the config's directory starts with ../ and never equals manifestPath.\n- The function adds no imports.\n- The function uses strings, whose import is owned by another declaration in the same file.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func mergeIsAutomatic(r *repo, treeID string, parents []string) bool {\\n\\tif len(parents) != 2 {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tautoTree, conflicts, err := autoMergeTree(r, parents[0], parents[1])\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tout, err := r.git(\\\"diff-tree\\\", \\\"-r\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", \\\"--no-renames\\\", autoTree, treeID)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\tvar diffPaths []string\\n\\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(out, \\\"\\\\n\\\") {\\n\\t\\tif line != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tdiffPaths = append(diffPaths, line)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tif len(diffPaths) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn true\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, p := range diffPaths {\\n\\t\\tif p != manifestPath {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, c := range conflicts {\\n\\t\\tif c == manifestPath {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn true\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn false\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"name\":\"mergeIsAutomatic\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"errors\"} (owned by prov-2026-0cd78a69; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"} (owned by prov-2026-0cd78a69; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-0cd78a69; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-25b92cac; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"} (owned by prov-2026-25b92cac; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"name\":\"commitParents\"} (owned by prov-2026-06e21d9f; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"name\":\"autoMergeTree\"} (owned by prov-2026-0cd78a69; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go\",\"name\":\"pendingMergeParents\"} (owned by prov-2026-25b92cac; do not select)\n\n## Files\n\nThese files exist and are the only ones the actions below may reach:\n\n- cmd/provenance/merge_exempt_run.go (package go; injection points: decls, imports)\n\n## Actions\n\n{\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"addImport\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Imports one package.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The import path.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"imports\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"path\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setConst\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one package-level constant, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole const declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The constant's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\