time=2026-10-26T16:28:09.687Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-6af220a3 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe commitFiles function lists the paths a commit changes relative to every one of its parents.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives a pointer to a repo and a commit revision string, in that order\n- The function returns a slice of strings and an error, in that order\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The function runs git through the repo git method (defined in common_run.go; variadic string parameters; returns trimmed standard output and an error)\n- The function first runs the git subcommand rev-list with the arguments --parents, -n, 1 and the revision, in that order\n- When that command fails the function returns a nil slice and its error\n- For a commit without parents the output of diff-tree is split on any whitespace into the set of paths\n- For a commit with parents the output of each diff-tree is split on newlines into a set of paths and empty lines are ignored\n- When any diff-tree command fails the function returns a nil slice and its error\n- The result is sorted in ascending order by plain string comparison\n- The result is a nil slice when no path qualifies and the error is then nil\n- The function owns the imports of sort and strings, each as a value import of the standard library\n- The output of the rev-list command is split on whitespace into fields\n- The first field of the rev-list output, which is the commit's own id, is dropped\n- The remaining fields of the rev-list output are the parents, in the order git lists them\n- The result holds the paths that are present in every one of the sets built above\n- For a commit without parents the function runs diff-tree with the arguments --root, --no-commit-id, --name-only, -r, --no-renames, --relative and the revision, in that order.\n- For a commit with parents the function runs, once per parent in order, diff-tree with the arguments --no-commit-id, --name-only, -r, --no-renames, --relative, the parent id and the revision, in that order.\n- The --relative argument makes diff-tree print each path relative to the directory git runs in, which is the repo root, namely the config's directory.\n- The --relative argument makes diff-tree leave out every changed path outside that directory.\n- When the config's directory is the git top level, the paths are the same as without --relative.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"sort\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func commitFiles(r *repo, rev string) ([]string, error) {\\n\\tout, err := r.git(\\\"rev-list\\\", \\\"--parents\\\", \\\"-n\\\", \\\"1\\\", rev)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tfields := strings.Fields(out)\\n\\tvar sets []map[string]bool\\n\\tif len(fields) \\u003c= 1 {\\n\\t\\tout, err := r.git(\\\"diff-tree\\\", \\\"--root\\\", \\\"--no-commit-id\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", \\\"-r\\\", \\\"--no-renames\\\", rev)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tset := map[string]bool{}\\n\\t\\tfor _, p := range strings.Fields(out) {\\n\\t\\t\\tset[p] = true\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tsets = append(sets, set)\\n\\t} else {\\n\\t\\tfor _, parent := range fields[1:] {\\n\\t\\t\\tout, err := r.git(\\\"diff-tree\\\", \\\"--no-commit-id\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", \\\"-r\\\", \\\"--no-renames\\\", parent, rev)\\n\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tset := map[string]bool{}\\n\\t\\t\\tfor _, p := range strings.Split(out, \\\"\\\\n\\\") {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif p != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tset[p] = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tsets = append(sets, set)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tcounts := map[string]int{}\\n\\tfor _, set := range sets {\\n\\t\\tfor p := range set {\\n\\t\\t\\tcounts[p]++\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tvar result []string\\n\\tfor p, n := range counts {\\n\\t\\tif n == len(sets) {\\n\\t\\t\\tresult = append(result, p)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tsort.Strings(result)\\n\\treturn result, nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"commitFiles\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"io\"} (owned by prov-2026-5577cfa8; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"bytes\"} (owned by prov-2026-d741e072; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"fmt\"} (owned by prov-2026-d741e072; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-d741e072; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"} (owned by prov-2026-d741e072; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"runCheckCommits\"} (owned by prov-2026-5577cfa8; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"checkCommit\"} (owned by prov-2026-1d77499a; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"commitTree\"} (owned by prov-2026-d741e072; do not select)\n\n## Files\n\nThese files exist and are the only ones the actions below may reach:\n\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go (package go; injection points: decls, imports)\n\n## Actions\n\n{\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"addImport\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Imports one package.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The import path.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"imports\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"path\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setConst\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one package-level constant, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole const declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The constant's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setFunction\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one top-level function, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole function declaration, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The function's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setMethod\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one method, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole method declaration, receiver, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\":