time=2026-10-26T16:28:18.068Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-8a4ab260 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe checkChange function checks a change between a base revision and a tree against the records and the commit message, returning every violation.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives, in order: a pointer to a repo, the base revision string, the tree path string, a slice of changed path strings and the commit message string\n- The function returns a slice of violation and an error\n- The function builds a store over the tree that is a record.FilesStore\n- The store's Root is set to the tree\n- The store's Dir is set to the repo's Config.Dir\n- The store's SpecRoot is set to the tree\n- For each changed path in order, the function takes the snapshot owner from snapshotOwner (parameters: a pointer to a repo and a path string; returns a string)\n- A violation is added only when the owner is non-empty\n- A violation is added only when headHas (parameters: a pointer to a repo, a revision string and a path string; returns a boolean) says the path exists at the base\n- A violation is added only when pinLogAppendOnly (parameters: a pointer to a repo, the base string, the tree string and the path string; returns a boolean) returns false\n- That violation's RecordID is the owner\n- That violation's File is empty\n- That violation's Message is \"snapshot files are append-only: \" followed by the path, \" already exists in \" and the base revision\n- For each changed path, the record id comes from recordFileID (parameters: a pointer to a repo and a path string; returns a string)\n- Paths with an empty id are skipped in the status check\n- A record file that does not exist in the tree is skipped in the status check\n- A record file that fails to load from the staged store (Load takes an id string and returns a record pointer, a document pointer and an error) is skipped in the status check\n- The status check loads the record at the base with headRecord (parameters: a pointer to a repo, a revision string and a path string; returns a pointer to a record.Record and a boolean)\n- The status check applies only when the base record exists\n- The status check applies only when the base record's Schema is 2\n- The status check applies only when the base record's Status differs from the staged record's Status\n- When CheckTransition returns an error, a violation is added\n- That violation's RecordID is the record id\n- That violation's File is empty\n- That violation's Message is the id, a colon, a space and the error text\n- The enforcement level is the repo's Config.Enforcement, or \"none\" when that is empty\n- The function loads shared records with loadShared (shared_run.go; parameter: a pointer to a repo; returns a map of record id to record pointer and a slice of warning strings)\n- The warnings returned by loadShared are ignored\n- The function lints the staged store with lint.Lint (parameters in order: the store and a lint.Options struct; returns a result pointer and an error)\n- The lint result has an Issues slice\n- The lint options field Root is the tree\n- The lint options field Enforcement is the enforcement level above\n- The lint options field ExcludePaths is the repo's Config.ExcludePaths\n- The lint options field ManifestPath is the manifestPath constant (common_run.go, a string)\n- The lint options field Shared is the loaded shared records\n- The lint options field SharedRepos is the result of sharedNames (shared_run.go; parameter: a pointer to a repo; returns a slice of strings)\n- When linting fails, the function returns a nil slice and the error\n- The function parses commit tags from the message with lint.ParseCommitTags (parameter: the message string; returns a slice of lint.Tag, each with a string field ID, an integer field Version that is 0 for an unversioned tag, and a String method)\n- An issue is relevant when its record id is the id of a tag\n- An issue is relevant when its record id is the id of a changed record file\n- Each element of the Issues slice has string fields Rule, RecordID and Message and a Severity of type lint.Severity\n- For each lint issue with error severity (lint.SeverityError) whose RecordID is empty or relevant, a violation is added\n- That violation's RecordID is the issue's RecordID\n- That violation's File is empty\n- That violation's Message is \"lint \" followed by the issue's Rule, a colon, a space and the issue's Message\n- A changed path is non-excluded only when scope.Excluded (parameters: a path string and a slice of exclude patterns; returns a boolean) is false for it with the repo's Config.ExcludePaths\n- A changed path is non-excluded only when stateExempt (parameters: a pointer to a repo and a path string; returns a boolean) is false for it\n- When the message has no tags, the repo's Config.CommitTagRequired is true and there is at least one non-excluded path, a violation is added\n- That violation's RecordID is empty\n- That violation's File is empty\n- That violation's Message is \"Commit tag required but no provenance ID found in message\"\n- When the message has no tags, the function returns the violations gathered so far and a nil error\n- When there are tags but no non-excluded path, the function returns the violations gathered so far and a nil error\n- Each tag is processed in order by resolving it with lint.ResolveTag (parameters: the staged store and the tag; returns a resolved value with a string ID field, and an error)\n- When resolving fails for an unversioned tag, the tag is skipped\n- When resolving fails for a versioned tag, a violation is added\n- That violation's RecordID is the tag's ID\n- That violation's File is empty\n- That violation's Message is the error text\n- After that violation the tag is skipped\n- The resolved record is loaded from the staged store by the resolved ID\n- When loading the resolved record fails, the tag is skipped\n- When the tag has a version and it differs from the loaded record's Version, a violation is added\n- That violation's RecordID is the record's id\n- That violation's File is empty\n- That violation's Message is \"<id> is at version <version> in this commit: tag it [<id>@<version>], not <tag text>\"\n- <tag text> in that Message is the tag's String result\n- After that violation the tag is skipped\n- The record's own file is the Config.Dir, a slash, the record id and \".yml\"\n- The paths to enforce are the non-excluded paths in order, minus the exempt ones listed next\n- The manifest path (manifestPath) is exempt\n- Version snapshot files whose snapshot owner is the tagged record are exempt\n- The record's own file is exempt only when the base record exists\n- The record's own file is exempt only when the base record has the same Status as the staged record\n- The record's own file is exempt only when the base record has the same Version as the staged record\n- The record's own file is exempt only when the base record has a different ImplementsVersion\n- A record file whose record, loaded from the staged store, has Implements equal to the tagged record's id is exempt\n- regenerationOnly is defined in regen_run.go; its parameters in order are a pointer to a repo, the base string, the tree string, a slice of path strings and a pointer to the tagged record; it returns a boolean\n- regenerationOnly is called with every changed path, not only the paths to enforce\n- When the tagged record is implemented, the commit is not a completion commit and regenerationOnly returns false, a violation is added\n- That violation's RecordID is the record id\n- That violation's File is empty\n- After that violation the tag's remaining checks are skipped\n- When regenerationOnly returns true, the scope checks below still run for every path to enforce\n- For a path to enforce equal to the record's own file, each pattern of the record's ForbiddenScope is tried in order with scope.Match (parameters: path string and pattern string; returns a boolean and an error)\n- A match error on the record's own file makes the function return a nil slice and that error\n- The first forbidden pattern that matches the record's own file adds a violation\n- That violation's RecordID is the record id\n- That violation's File is the path\n- That violation's Message is \"<id> forbids changes to <path>\"\n- No further patterns are tried for that file once one has matched\n- The record's own file gets no in-scope check beyond its forbidden patterns\n- Every other path to enforce is tested with scope.InScope (parameters: a record pointer and a path string; returns a boolean and an error)\n- An InScope error makes the function return a nil slice and that error\n- A path that is not in scope is accepted when deletedFromPreviousScope (parameters in order: a pointer to a repo, the staged store pointer, the base string, the tree string, the record pointer, the path string; returns a boolean) returns true\n- Any other path that is not in scope adds a violation\n- That violation's RecordID is the record id\n- That violation's File is the path\n- That violation's Message is \"<id> forbids changes to <path>\"\n- After all tags are processed the function returns the violations and a nil error\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The repo's Config.Dir field is a string holding the records directory relative to the repo root, without a trailing slash\n- The repo's Config.Enforcement field is a string\n- The repo's Config.ExcludePaths field is a slice of strings\n- The repo's Config.CommitTagRequired field is a boolean\n- The tag's Version is an integer and its String method takes no arguments and returns the tag text\n- The status check calls lint.CheckTransition (parameters in order: the previous status and the new status, both record.Status values passed as they are without any conversion, and a boolean that is true when the staged Version is greater than the base Version; returns an error)\n- The record.Record fields relied on are: Schema and Version and ImplementsVersion are integers, ID and Implements are strings, Status is the record package's Status type compared with record.StatusImplemented, and ForbiddenScope is a slice of strings\n- The two statuses given to lint.CheckTransition keep their record.Status type and are never converted to string or any other type\n- A commit is a completion commit only when it stages the record's own file and, at the same time, the record's base version exists with a Status other than implemented; either condition alone does not make it one\n- When no path remains to enforce, the tag is skipped before the implemented-record check is made, so a tag whose paths are all exempt is never refused as implemented\n- sedumMissing is defined in regen_run.go; it takes no parameters and returns a boolean\n- sedumMissing is called only when the implemented-record violation is about to be added, after regenerationOnly has returned false\n- When sedumMissing returns false, the implemented-record violation's Message is \"<id> is implemented: run 'provenance revise <id>' to start a new version, then tag the commit with it.\"\n- When sedumMissing returns true, the implemented-record violation's Message is \"<id> regeneration check could not run sedum: not found on PATH; set SEDUM_BIN or install sedum (if this is not a regeneration commit, run 'provenance revise <id>' to start a new version, then tag the commit with it)\"\n- The implemented-record violation's Message always begins with the record id\n- The changed paths are slash-separated and relative to the config's directory, and the tree path is the directory that holds the config's files at that same layout.\n- The function owns the imports of github.com/livecodelife/provenance/lint and github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope, each as a value import of a package of this module\n- The function uses fmt and the record package, whose imports are owned by other records in the same file\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/lint\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func checkChange(r *repo, base, tree string, changed []string, message string) ([]violation, error) {\\n\\tstore := \\u0026record.FilesStore{Root: tree, Dir: r.Config.Dir, SpecRoot: tree}\\n\\tshared, _ := loadShared(r)\\n\\tenforcement := r.Config.Enforcement\\n\\tif enforcement == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tenforcement = \\\"none\\\"\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar out []violation\\n\\tfor _, p := range changed {\\n\\t\\towner := snapshotOwner(r, p)\\n\\t\\tif owner == \\\"\\\" || !headHas(r, base, p) || pinLogAppendOnly(r, base, tree, p) {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: owner, Message: \\\"snapshot files are append-only: \\\" + p + \\\" already exists in \\\" + base})\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tfor _, p := range changed {\\n\\t\\tid := recordFileID(r, p)\\n\\t\\tif id == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tstaged, _, err := store.Load(id)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\told, ok := headRecord(r, base, p)\\n\\t\\tif !ok || old == nil || old.Schema != 2 || old.Status == staged.Status {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif err := lint.CheckTransition(old.Status, staged.Status, staged.Version \\u003e old.Version); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: id, Message: id + \\\": \\\" + err.Error()})\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tres, err := lint.Lint(store, lint.Options{\\n\\t\\tRoot:         tree,\\n\\t\\tEnforcement:  enforcement,\\n\\t\\tExcludePaths: r.Config.ExcludePaths,\\n\\t\\tManifestPath: manifestPath,\\n\\t\\tShared:       shared,\\n\\t\\tSharedRepos:  sharedNames(r),\\n\\t})\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\ttags := lint.ParseCommitTags(message)\\n\\ttagIDs := map[string]bool{}\\n\\tfor _, t := range tags {\\n\\t\\ttagIDs[t.ID] = true\\n\\t}\\n\\tchangedIDs := map[string]bool{}\\n\\tfor _, p := range changed {\\n\\t\\tif id := recordFileID(r, p); id != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tchangedIDs[id] = true\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, is := range res.Issues {\\n\\t\\tif is.Severity != lint.SeverityError {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif is.RecordID != \\\"\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 !tagIDs[is.RecordID] \\u0026\\u0026 !changedIDs[is.RecordID] {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: is.RecordID, Message: \\\"lint \\\" + is.Rule + \\\": \\\" + is.Message})\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar nonExcluded []string\\n\\tfor _, p := range changed {\\n\\t\\tif scope.Excluded(p, r.Config.ExcludePaths) || stateExempt(r, p) {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tnonExcluded = append(nonExcluded, p)\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif len(tags) == 0 {\\n\\t\\tif r.Config.CommitTagRequired \\u0026\\u0026 len(nonExcluded) \\u003e 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{Message: \\\"Commit tag required but no provenance ID found in message\\\"})\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn out, nil\\n\\t}\\n\\tif len(nonExcluded) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn out, nil\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tfor _, tag := range tags {\\n\\t\\tresolved, err := lint.ResolveTag(store, tag)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tif tag.Version == 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: tag.ID, Message: err.Error()})\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\trec, _, err := store.Load(resolved.ID)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif tag.Version != 0 \\u0026\\u0026 tag.Version != rec.Version {\\n\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: rec.ID, Message: fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%s is at version %d in this commit: tag it [%s@%d], not %s\\\", rec.ID, rec.Version, rec.ID, rec.Version, tag.String())})\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\town := r.Config.Dir + \\\"/\\\" + rec.ID + \\\".yml\\\"\\n\\t\\tbaseOwn, hasBaseOwn := headRecord(r, base, own)\\n\\t\\tvar enforce []string\\n\\t\\tfor _, p := range nonExcluded {\\n\\t\\t\\tif p == manifestPath {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif owner := snapshotOwner(r, p); owner == rec.ID {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif p == own \\u0026\\u0026 hasBaseOwn \\u0026\\u0026 baseOwn != nil \\u0026\\u0026 baseOwn.Status == rec.Status \\u0026\\u0026 baseOwn.Version == rec.Version \\u0026\\u0026 baseOwn.ImplementsVersion != rec.ImplementsVersion {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif id := recordFileID(r, p); id != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif other, _, err := store.Load(id); err == nil \\u0026\\u0026 other.Implements == rec.ID {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tenforce = append(enforce, p)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif len(enforce) == 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\tstagesOwn := false\\n\\t\\tfor _, p := range changed {\\n\\t\\t\\tif p == own {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tstagesOwn = true\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tcompletion := stagesOwn \\u0026\\u0026 hasBaseOwn \\u0026\\u0026 baseOwn != nil \\u0026\\u0026 baseOwn.Status != record.StatusImplemented\\n\\t\\tif rec.Status == record.StatusImplemented \\u0026\\u0026 !completion \\u0026\\u0026 !regenerationOnly(r, base, tree, changed, rec) {\\n\\t\\t\\tmsg := rec.ID + \\\" is implemented: run 'provenance revise \\\" + rec.ID + \\\"' to start a new version, then tag the commit with it.\\\"\\n\\t\\t\\tif sedumMissing() {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tmsg = rec.ID + \\\" regeneration check could not run sedum: not found on PATH; set SEDUM_BIN or install sedum (if this is not a regeneration commit, run 'provenance revise \\\" + rec.ID + \\\"' to start a new version, then tag the commit with it)\\\"\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: rec.ID, Message: msg})\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\tfor _, p := range enforce {\\n\\t\\t\\tif p == own {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor _, pat := range rec.ForbiddenScope {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tmatched, err := scope.Match(p, pat)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif matched {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: rec.ID, File: p, Message: rec.ID + \\\" forbids changes to \\\" + p})\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tin, err := scope.InScope(rec, p)\\n\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif in {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif deletedFromPreviousScope(r, store, base, tree, rec, p) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tout = append(out, violation{RecordID: rec.ID, File: p, Message: rec.ID + \\\" forbids changes to \\\" + p})\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\treturn out, nil\\n}\\n\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"name\":\"checkChange\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-28d0e0c4; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"errors\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"fmt\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-7e91a9e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"io\"} (owned by prov-2026-95bdf404; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record\"} (owned by prov-2026-aa14b7e3; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"} (owned by prov-2026-da957222; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"name\":\"headHas\"} (owned by prov-2026-15cd7313; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"name\":\"stagedTree\"} (owned by prov-2026-28d0e0c4; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_run.go: setType {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_run.go\",\"name\":\"violation\"} (owned by prov-2026-32011b