time=2026-10-26T16:28:41.876Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-cbd32da5 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe stagedPaths function lists the paths changed in the index, leaving out paths that only came from a merge.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives a pointer to a repo as its only argument\n- The function returns a slice of strings and an error\n- When git fails, the function returns a nil slice and the error\n- The output is split on newline characters\n- Empty lines are dropped\n- The order of the paths is the order git printed them\n- The function passes the paths through mergeFiltered (defined in this file; parameters in order: a pointer to a repo and a slice of strings; returns a slice of strings)\n- The function returns mergeFiltered's result as the paths\n- The function returns a nil error on success\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The repo's git method takes a variadic list of string arguments, runs git in the repo root and returns the trimmed standard output as a string and an error\n- The function adds no imports\n- The function runs the repo's git method (variadic string arguments; returns trimmed standard output and an error) with diff, --cached, --name-only, --no-renames and --relative.\n- The --relative argument makes git print each path relative to the directory git runs in, which is the repo root, namely the config's directory.\n- The --relative argument makes git leave out every changed path outside that directory.\n- When the config's directory is the git top level, the paths are the same as without --relative.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku g