time=2026-10-26T16:28:47.794Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-d741e072 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe commitTree function extracts a commit's files into a fresh temporary directory.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives a pointer to a repo and a commit revision string, in that order\n- The function returns the directory path as a string, a cleanup function with no parameters and no result, and an error, in that order\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The function creates a new directory with os.MkdirTemp in the default temporary directory with the name prefix provenance-commit-\n- When the directory cannot be created the function returns an empty string, a nil cleanup function and that error\n- The repo root, the revision and the directory are passed to the shell script as positional arguments and not spliced into the script text\n- The command environment is the slice returned by the repo gitEnv method (defined in common_run.go; no parameters; returns a slice of strings)\n- The command's standard error is captured in a bytes.Buffer\n- When the command fails the function removes the new directory and all its content\n- When the command fails the function returns an empty string, a nil cleanup function and a non-nil error\n- The error text on failure is the text git archive followed by a space, then the revision, then a colon and a space, then the command's own error text, then a newline, then the captured standard error\n- The error on failure wraps the command's own error\n- On success the function returns the directory, a cleanup function that removes the directory and all its content, and a nil error\n- The function owns the imports of bytes, fmt, os and os/exec, each as a value import of the standard library\n- The function runs a shell through os/exec with the arguments sh and -c followed by a script\n- The script pipes the output of git -C with the repo root and archive with the revision into tar extracting into the new directory\n- The shell is given three extra arguments in this order: the repo root (the repo's Root field) first, then the revision, then the new directory\n- Because git archive runs in the repo root, the extracted directory holds only the files under that directory, at paths relative to it.\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"bytes\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"fmt\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func commitTree(r *repo, rev string) (string, func(), error) {\\n\\tdir, err := os.MkdirTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"provenance-commit-\\\")\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tscript := `git -C \\\"$1\\\" archive \\\"$2\\\" | tar -x -C \\\"$3\\\"`\\n\\tcmd := exec.Command(\\\"sh\\\", \\\"-c\\\", script, \\\"sh\\\", r.Root, rev, dir)\\n\\tcmd.Env = r.gitEnv()\\n\\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\\n\\tcmd.Stderr = \\u0026stderr\\n\\tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tos.RemoveAll(dir)\\n\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"git archive %s: %w\\\\n%s\\\", rev, err, stderr.String())\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn dir, func() { os.RemoveAll(dir) }, nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"commitTree\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"io\"} (owned by prov-2026-5577cfa8; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"sort\"} (owned by prov-2026-6af220a3; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-6af220a3; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"runCheckCommits\"} (owned by prov-2026-5577cfa8; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"checkCommit\"} (owned by prov-2026-1d77499a; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/check_commits_run.go\",\"name\":\"commitFiles\"} (owned by prov-2026-6af220a3; do