time=2026-10-26T16:29:02.651Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-f86ede24 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe regenerationOnly function reports whether a change is a pure re-render of sedum regions in governed files, with no change to record state.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives, in order: a pointer to a repo, the base revision string, the tree path string, a slice of all changed path strings and a pointer to the tagged record.Record\n- The function returns a boolean\n- The tagged record parameter is not used.\n- The function returns false when any changed path is a record file (recordFileID, check_run.go; parameters: a pointer to a repo and a path string; returns a string, non-empty for a record file)\n- The function returns false when stateExempt (check_run.go; parameters: a pointer to a repo and a path string; returns a boolean) is true for any changed path\n- Changed paths for which scope.Excluded (parameters: a path string and the repo's Config.ExcludePaths slice; returns a boolean) is true are ignored by the remaining steps\n- The function returns false when no governed path remains\n- For each governed path the function returns false when headHas (check_run.go; parameters: a pointer to a repo, a revision string and a path string; returns a boolean) says it is absent from the base\n- The staged file of a governed path is the tree path joined with the changed path converted to the operating system's separator\n- The function returns false when the staged file does not exist or cannot be read\n- The git command runs with the repo's Root as working directory\n- The git command's environment is the result of the repo's gitEnv method\n- The base content is the raw output bytes, untrimmed\n- The function returns false when the base content cannot be read\n- The function returns false when regionsAgree (parameters: base content string and staged content string; returns a boolean) is false for any governed path\n- The records to verify are the distinct record ids named by the regions of the staged content of the governed paths, in order of first appearance\n- The function returns false unless sedumCurrent (parameters: a pointer to a repo, the tree string and a record id string; returns a boolean) is true for each of those ids\n- The function returns true when all steps pass\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main\n- The repo's Root field is a string holding the absolute repository root path\n- The repo's Config.ExcludePaths field is a slice of strings\n- The repo's gitEnv method takes no arguments and returns the environment for git commands as a slice of strings\n- The function reads those ids by splitting the staged content with splitRegions (parameter: a string; returns outside text, a slice of regionMarker values and a boolean) and taking the Record field of each marker; a regionMarker has only the fields Tier, Record and Gen\n- The function never refers to an ID field of a regionMarker because it has none\n- The base content is read by running git cat-file blob with the base, a colon, ./ and the path.\n- The ./ before the path makes git resolve the path relative to the repo root, which is the git command's working directory, rather than the git top level.\n- The function owns the imports of github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record and github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope, each as a value import of a package of this module\n- The function uses os, os/exec and path/filepath, whose imports are owned by another record in the same file\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/scope\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func regenerationOnly(r *repo, base string, treePath string, changed []string, _ *record.Record) bool {\\n\\tvar governed []string\\n\\tfor _, p := range changed {\\n\\t\\tif recordFileID(r, p) != \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif stateExempt(r, p) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif scope.Excluded(p, r.Config.ExcludePaths) {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tgoverned = append(governed, p)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif len(governed) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar stagedAll []string\\n\\tfor _, p := range governed {\\n\\t\\tif !headHas(r, base, p) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tstaged := filepath.Join(treePath, filepath.FromSlash(p))\\n\\t\\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(staged)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tcmd := exec.Command(\\\"git\\\", \\\"cat-file\\\", \\\"blob\\\", base+\\\":\\\"+p)\\n\\t\\tcmd.Dir = r.Root\\n\\t\\tcmd.Env = r.gitEnv()\\n\\t\\tbaseOut, err := cmd.Output()\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif !regionsAgree(string(baseOut), string(data)) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tstagedAll = append(stagedAll, string(data))\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tseen := map[string]bool{}\\n\\tvar ids []string\\n\\tfor _, content := range stagedAll {\\n\\t\\t_, markers, _ := splitRegions(content)\\n\\t\\tfor _, m := range markers {\\n\\t\\t\\tif !seen[m.Record] {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tseen[m.Record] = true\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids = append(ids, m.Record)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tfor _, id := range ids {\\n\\t\\tif !sedumCurrent(r, treePath, id) {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn true\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"regenerationOnly\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"os/exec\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: addImport {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"path\":\"strings\"} (owned by prov-2026-351c5684; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"splitRegions\"} (owned by prov-2026-0b95d9fb; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setFunction {\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/regen_run.go\",\"name\":\"regionsAgree\"} (owned by prov-2026-342fc2b3; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/regen_run.go: setFunction {